@startuml 02-state-machines
!include _style.puml
title **Procurement & Materials - State Machines**\nEvery transition below is enforced in code by a transition table, not by an if-statement

' =====================================================================
'  MATERIAL REQUISITION
' =====================================================================
state "Material Requisition  (MR)" as MRBOX {
  state DRAFT #1e3a5f
  state SUBMITTED
  state TECHNICAL_APPROVED
  state APPROVED #14532d
  state ORDERED #14532d
  state REJECTED #7f1d1d

  [*] --> DRAFT : raiseRequisition()\n<<buyer types: EPC, SUB, OWN>>
  DRAFT --> SUBMITTED : submitRequisition()
  SUBMITTED --> TECHNICAL_APPROVED : approveTechnically()\n<<SoD: approver != raiser>>
  TECHNICAL_APPROVED --> APPROVED : approveCommercially()\n<<SoD: commercial != technical>>
  APPROVED --> ORDERED : createPurchaseOrder()
  SUBMITTED --> REJECTED : rejectRequisition()\n<<reason mandatory>>
  TECHNICAL_APPROVED --> REJECTED : rejectRequisition()
  REJECTED --> DRAFT : rework
  ORDERED --> [*]

  note right of REJECTED
    Rejection is **not** terminal.
    Real requisitions come back with a
    corrected spec. The reason text is
    mandatory, and survives the rework
    so the second reviewer can see what
    the first one objected to.
  end note
}

' =====================================================================
'  PURCHASE ORDER
' =====================================================================
state "Purchase Order  (PO)" as POBOX {
  state PO_DRAFT as "DRAFT" #1e3a5f
  state ISSUED
  state PARTIALLY_RECEIVED
  state RECEIVED #14532d
  state CANCELLED #7f1d1d

  [*] --> PO_DRAFT : createPurchaseOrder()\n<<MR must be APPROVED>>
  PO_DRAFT --> ISSUED : issuePurchaseOrder()\n<<MR -> ORDERED>>
  ISSUED --> PARTIALLY_RECEIVED : receive() partial
  ISSUED --> RECEIVED : receive() in full
  PARTIALLY_RECEIVED --> RECEIVED : receive() balance
  PARTIALLY_RECEIVED --> PARTIALLY_RECEIVED : receive() more
  RECEIVED --> PARTIALLY_RECEIVED : reverse() a GRN
  PO_DRAFT --> CANCELLED
  ISSUED --> CANCELLED
  PARTIALLY_RECEIVED --> CANCELLED
  RECEIVED --> [*]

  note right of PARTIALLY_RECEIVED
    **Derived, never set.**
    refreshPurchaseOrderState() recomputes
    this from the movement ledger after every
    receipt and every reversal. No caller may
    nudge a PO into RECEIVED by hand.

    Hence RECEIVED -> PARTIALLY_RECEIVED: reversing
    a goods receipt must be able to walk the
    state backwards, or the ledger and the
    header would disagree.
  end note

  note bottom of ISSUED
    acceptsReceipts() is true only for
    ISSUED and PARTIALLY_RECEIVED.
    You cannot book stock against a
    draft or a cancelled order.
  end note
}

' =====================================================================
'  MATERIAL LOT - physical custody
' =====================================================================
state "Material Lot  -  physical custody" as LOTBOX {
  state "Ordered (not yet arrived)" as ORD #1e3a5f
  state "In store" as STORE
  state "Issued to fabrication" as ISS
  state "Installed on site" as SITE #14532d

  [*] --> ORD
  ORD --> STORE : **receive()**  GRN\nsign +1
  STORE --> ISS : **issue()**  MIV\nsign -1
  ISS --> SITE : **deliverToSite()**  SDN\nsign **0**
  ISS --> STORE : **returnToStore()**  MRN\nsign +1
  STORE --> STORE : reverse() a GRN
  SITE --> [*]

  note right of ISS
    **ISSUE and SITE are two steps, deliberately.**

    ISSUE answers a *stock* question - the material
    has left the warehouse. SITE answers a
    *completion* question - it is installed in a
    subsystem.

    Between them sits the laydown area, where
    material can sit for weeks. Collapsing the two
    would make that material invisible: gone from
    stock, not yet counted as progress.

    That is why **SDN carries sign 0** - the stock
    already left at MIV. Counting it twice would
    drive the balance negative.
  end note
}

legend right
  |= colour |= meaning |
  |<#1e3a5f>| initial / not yet committed |
  |<#1e293b>| in flight |
  |<#14532d>| successful terminal |
  |<#7f1d1d>| refused / cancelled |
endlegend

@enduml
